.Dd November 25, 2026
.Dt SUBSTRINGS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm substrings
.Nd suffix array text analysis tool
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Op Fl -
.Op Ar file
.Nm
.Fl -inline
.Op Ar options
.Op Fl -
.Ar text
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
builds the suffix array of a text and prints its most frequent repeated
substrings, sorted by frequency and then lexicographically, one per line as
.Dq Ar substring count .
It can also count the occurrences of given patterns, find palindromes and
shortest unique substrings, compute the
LZ77 factorization and the Burrows\(enWheeler transform, show the internal
suffix array tables, and write the suffix tree as a Graphviz file.
.Pp
The input is the contents of
.Ar file ,
given as the argument or with
.Fl i ,
or standard input if there is none or it is
.Ql - .
With
.Fl -inline ,
the argument is the
.Ar text
itself.
An argument that starts with
.Ql -
must follow
.Fl - .
Inputs are treated as bytes; results never split a UTF\-8 character, and
lengths and positions of palindromes and unique substrings count characters.
.Pp
When standard error is a terminal and building the suffix array takes more
than a moment, a progress bar is shown there.
.Sh OPTIONS
Options with a value take it after
.Ql =
or as the next argument, except
.Fl -color ,
which needs
.Ql = .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl i Ar file , Fl -input Ns = Ns Ar file
Read the input from
.Ar file ,
or from standard input if it is
.Ql - .
.It Fl -inline
Take the argument as the input text instead of a file name.
.It Fl o Ar file , Fl -output Ns = Ns Ar file
Write the output to
.Ar file
instead of standard output, unless it is
.Ql - .
.It Fl n Ar N , Fl -top Ns = Ns Ar N
Print at most
.Ar N
repeated substrings.
The default is 100000.
.It Fl -minlength Ns = Ns Ar N
Print only repeated substrings of at least
.Ar N
bytes, or with
.Fl -words ,
phrases of at least
.Ar N
words.
The default is 2 bytes, or 1 word.
.It Fl -words
List only whole words and phrases: repeats that start and end at a word
boundary, counted only where they do, so
.Ql the
inside
.Ql other
does not count.
A word is a run of letters and digits: ASCII letters and digits, and every
character from U+00C0 on except U+2000\(enU+2FFF (punctuation, quotes,
dashes and symbols).
Anything else separates words, and phrases keep it:
.Ql don't
is the two words
.Ql don
and
.Ql t ,
and also a phrase.
With
.Fl -find ,
count only the occurrences that are whole words or phrases.
.It Fl -nocount
Omit the occurrence counts.
.It Fl -delimiter Ns = Ns Ar str
Separate a substring from its count with
.Ar str
instead of a space.
.It Fl -entry-delimiter Ns = Ns Ar str
Separate entries with
.Ar str
instead of a newline.
Both delimiters accept the escapes
.Ql \en ,
.Ql \er ,
.Ql \et ,
.Ql \e\e
and
.Ql \e0 .
.It Fl -find Ns = Ns Ar pattern
Instead of the repeats, print
.Ar pattern
and its number of occurrences, in the same format.
Repeat the option to count several patterns.
.Ar pattern
accepts the same escapes as the delimiters, so
.Fl -find Ns = Ns Ql \er\en
counts line breaks.
.It Fl -escape Ns Op = Ns Ar when
Escape line breaks, tabs, other control characters, invisible characters and
invalid UTF\-8 in the repeats, patterns, palindromes and unique substrings
as
.Ql \en ,
.Ql \et ,
.Ql \exNN ,
.Ql \euXXXX ,
and backslashes as
.Ql \e\e ,
so that every result stays on one line:
.Cm auto
(the default) when writing to a terminal,
.Cm always
(also
.Fl -escape
alone) or
.Cm never .
.It Fl -json
Print the repeats, pattern counts, palindromes and shortest unique
substrings as JSON Lines;
see
.Sx JSON OUTPUT .
.Fl -nocount
and the delimiters are ignored.
Not available with
.Fl -lz77 ,
.Fl -bwt
or
.Fl -view-internal-tables .
.It Fl -palindrome
Before the repeats, print the distinct maximal palindromes, longest first
(up to 1000).
.It Fl -shortest-unique
Before the repeats, print every shortest substring that occurs exactly once
(up to 1000).
.It Fl -lz77
Instead of the repeats, print the greedy LZ77 factorization as
tab-separated values: one
.Ql pos len src text
line per phrase
.Ql ( src
is
.Ql -
for a literal byte), then a
.Ql #
summary line.
The text column is escaped reversibly, so the input can be rebuilt from the
output.
.It Fl -bwt
Instead of the repeats, print the Burrows\(enWheeler matrix of the input
followed by
.Ql $ ,
the transform, the row of the original text and the number of runs.
The matrix is drawn only for inputs up to 1000 characters.
.It Fl -view-internal-tables
Instead of the repeats, print the SA, Rank, PLCP and LCP arrays next to the
sorted suffixes.
Control characters, invisible characters and invalid UTF\-8 are shown as
visible symbols or escapes.
.It Fl -graph
Write the suffix tree, with suffix links, to
.Pa suffix_tree.dot .
.It Fl -dotfile Ns = Ns Ar file
Write the suffix tree to
.Ar file .
Edge labels longer than 16 bytes are shortened.
.It Fl -force-graph
Allow
.Fl -graph
and
.Fl -dotfile
for inputs over 10 KB.
.It Fl -color Ns Op = Ns Ar when
Color the tables of
.Fl -bwt
and
.Fl -view-internal-tables :
.Cm auto
(the default) when writing to a terminal,
.Cm always
(also
.Fl -color
alone) or
.Cm never .
.It Fl -no-pager
Write to the terminal directly instead of through a pager.
.It Fl -completions Ns = Ns Ar shell
Print a completion script for
.Cm bash ,
.Cm zsh
or
.Cm fish
and exit.
.It Fl -version
Print the version and exit.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.El
.Sh JSON OUTPUT
With
.Fl -json ,
each result is one JSON object on its own line:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{"type":"repeat","text":"an","count":2}
{"type":"match","text":"an","count":2,"pos":[1,3]}
{"type":"palindrome","text":"anana","pos":1,"len":5}
{"type":"unique","text":"b","pos":0,"len":1}
{"type":"omitted","of":"palindrome","count":12}
.Ed
.Pp
.Ql pos
and
.Ql len
count characters; a
.Ql match
lists the positions of all occurrences.
Palindromes and unique substrings over 80 characters are abbreviated with
.Ql ...
in the middle, as in the plain output; an
.Ql omitted
object counts results past the first 1000.
Invalid UTF\-8 is replaced with U+FFFD.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev COLUMNS
The width that tables are fitted to, instead of the terminal's width
(80 when not writing to a terminal).
.It Ev LESS
Options for
.Xr less 1 .
If unset,
.Nm
runs the pager with
.Ev LESS Ns = Ns Ql FRX :
output that fits on one screen is printed directly, colors pass through, and
the screen is not cleared.
.It Ev SUBSTRINGS_PAGER , Ev PAGER
The pager for output to a terminal, run with
.Pa /bin/sh ;
.Ev SUBSTRINGS_PAGER
takes precedence.
The default is
.Xr less 1 .
An empty value or
.Ql cat
turns the pager off.
.It Ev NO_COLOR
If set to a non-empty value,
.Fl -color Ns = Ns Cm auto
does not color.
So does
.Ev TERM Ns = Ns Ql dumb .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Quitting the pager before all output is shown is not an error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
The ten most frequent repeats of at least 20 bytes:
.Pp
.Dl $ substrings -i pg100.txt --minlength=20 --top=10
.Pp
The most frequent phrases of at least four words:
.Pp
.Dl $ substrings -i pg100.txt --words --minlength=4 --top=20
.Pp
How often two words occur, and where one of them does:
.Pp
.Dl $ substrings -i pg100.txt --find=Hamlet --find=Ophelia
.Dl $ substrings -i pg100.txt --find=Ophelia --json | jq -c .pos
.Pp
Longest palindromes, as JSON:
.Pp
.Dl $ substrings --palindrome --json --top=1 -i text.txt | jq -r 'select(.type == \(dqpalindrome\(dq) | .text'
.Pp
The suffix tree of a short word, as a PDF:
.Pp
.Dl $ substrings --inline --graph banana && dot -Tpdf suffix_tree.dot -o tree.pdf
.Pp
Load completions in the current bash session:
.Pp
.Dl $ source <(substrings --completions=bash)
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dot 1 ,
.Xr less 1
.Pp
.Lk https://github.com/IlyaGrebnov/libsais libsais ,
which builds the suffix, PLCP and LCP arrays.
